    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: fe605f8eca51aed9e8f331e45b062be9bba77486 -->\nReview at head fe605f8ec. Read, not built: the PR is from a fork, and the run runner takes no fork code, and no local build slot was free.\n\nThe change since 7fc28eb9a:\n- `bf87523ad` splits the tooltip tests to the new `viewport_bar_tooltip_tests.rs` (321 lines) with a `#[path]` sibling mod. `viewport_bar_tests.rs` is back to 285 lines and `viewport_bar.rs` is 276. All files obey the 400-line rule. The earlier finding is met.\n- `fe605f8ec` merges main, and main now carries the merged PR #2783 - the same hover-help feature, in a static form. The hand resolution fuses the two: main's draw-list and hover-suppression code stands, and the PR's richer `tooltip(kind, state)` supplies the text (shortcut keys, the state-aware Display menu entries). `hover_text` and the drag/outside assertions from #2783's tests stand beside the PR's own paint tests. I read the remerge-diff: no side's lines were dropped. The screenshot generator's opt-in change survived.\n\nWhy the yellow label: the merge joined two live implementations of one feature by hand and no bot built the result. The read says it is right; the owner (or the merge batch's trial build) should confirm by compile before it goes green. Labels set: needs-rework and conflicts removed (both are false now), needs-maintainer added.\n",
